#X text 700 20 bridge_guiHub: the control-surface hub. REBUILDS the path the Max patch had via [gate 1] -> [js node.script ws_server.js] \, which was dropped to a doc comment during the Pd conversion (see CONVERSION_NOTES.md \, "New stand-in abstractions") -- taking with it the only route a GUI or the TUI had into or out of this patch. Talks to bridge/../gui/gui_hub_bridge.js \, a standalone Node process that also serves the panel over HTTP and WebSocket. Same architecture as the five existing bridges \, different job: this one carries no logic of its own \, it only relays., f 62;
#X text 700 190 INLET 0 -- TELEMETRY \, PATCH -> GUI. Send it an ordinary Pd message whose selector is the report name: "meter <stem> <peakL> <peakR> <rmsL> <rmsR>" \, "spectrum <stem> <64 floats>" \, "lufs <f>" \, "wave <stem> <min> <max>" \, "status <key> [args]". [pd packOSC] turns the selector into the OSC address and the rest into args -- the same proven subpatch bridge_slicer.pd and bridge_sliceWriter.pd use. The magnitudes go out LINEAR \, not in dB: Pd vanilla has no [log~] \, and the panel has to rescale for its own plot height anyway \, so the conversion lives in JS. See stem_telemetry~.pd for the objects that feed this., f 62;
#X text 700 400 OUTLET 0 (slicer) -> bridge_slicer's inlet. OUTLET 1 (analyze) -> bridge_analyzeReader's inlet \, the file-I/O/batch half. OUTLET 2 (reader) -> analyze_reader's inlet \, which is a DIFFERENT object -- the native-Pd rewrite that owns [route readVocals readMelo readBass readDrums set_track_name]. Those two are split on purpose: the names sit under one heading in GUI_PARAMETER_MAPPING.md and sending readVocals to the bridge reaches nothing at all. Each outlet carries a plain Pd list with the selector first \, e.g. "next drums" -- byte-identical to what the existing message boxes send into those same inlets \, which is why this hub needs no per-command knowledge. The FOURTH route outlet (patch) has no outlet object: it feeds the dynamic-send box [\\\; \$1 \$2] \, delivering "patch bpm 120" straight to [receive bpm]. That covers bpm \, record_cmd \, and the eight preview_rate_/preview_mute_ receives., f 62;
#X text 700 620 IMPORTANT -- do NOT put [list trim] in front of the dynamic-send box. [route] emits the remainder as a LIST \, so \$1 is the receive name and \$2 the value \, which is what the box needs. Trimming first would collapse "bpm 120" into a message with selector bpm \, making \$1 the value and \$2 empty -- silently sending nothing anywhere., f 62;
#X text 380 250 ports 9010 (in from Node) / 9011 (out to Node) -- clear of 9001 streamWatcher \, 9002-3 sliceWriter \, 9004-5 slicer \, 9006-7 analyzeReader \, 9008-9 bufferManager \, so all six run at once., f 40;
#X text 40 570 Start it alongside Pd: node src/gui/gui_hub_bridge.js --panel-dir src/gui --http-port 8080 --send-port 9010 --recv-port 9011 \, then open http://localhost:8080/panel.html, f 62;
